{
  "about": "Per-record aggregates: an aggregate's filter, range and derivations reduce only the records each row matches (LOOKUP-9, LOOKUP-22). Moved from execution_aggregate_record_operations.rs. The document spec is the test's specification() with no reduction written: each case's edit writes its reduction after the line that opens the aggregate, as the test's format! did. In ordered_converted_bindings_reduce_only_matched_filtered_inclusive_records, subject a keeps B's records with USE = 'Y' and N at most its CUT of 3: N = 2 and N = 3, whose V of 1.5 and 2 double to 3 and 4, so TOTAL is 7; b's one record converts nothing, so its V is the recovered 0; c has no CUT and d's CUT of 1 is below every N, so neither reduces a record and TOTAL is missing.",
  "documents": {
    "spec": "yamaa: \"1.0\"\ntype: spec\ndomain: TEST\nkeys: [ID]\ninput:\n  A: {path: a.csv, types: {CUT: int}}\n  B: {path: b.csv, key: [ID], types: {N: int}}\nbase: A\noutput: {path: result.csv, columns: [ID, CUT, TOTAL]}\ncolumns:\n  - {name: ID, type: str, derivation: A.ID}\n  - {name: CUT, type: int, derivation: A.CUT}\n  - name: TOTAL\n    type: float\n    derivation:\n      aggregate:\n",
    "rows": "yamaa: \"1.0\"\ntype: spec\ndomain: TEST\nkeys: [ID, ORIGIN]\ninput:\n  A: {path: a.csv, types: {CUT: int}}\n  B: {path: b.csv, key: [ID], types: {N: int}}\n  C: {path: c.csv, types: {LIMIT: int}}\noutput: {path: result.csv, columns: [ID, ORIGIN, TOTAL]}\ncolumns:\n  - {name: ID, type: str}\n  - {name: ORIGIN, type: str}\n  - name: TOTAL\n    type: float\n    derivation:\n      aggregate:\n        between: {value: A.CUT, lower: N}\n        expr: SUM(B.N)\nrows:\n  - id: a\n    dataset: A\n    derivations: {ID: A.ID, ORIGIN: \"'A'\"}\n"
  },
  "cases": [
